  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Plotting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#923;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></math> against <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>c&#923;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub></math> for aqueous solutions of a monobasic weak acid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>HX</mi><mo>)</mo></math> resulted in a straight line with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis intercept of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> and slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>. The ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>&nbsp;is<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#923;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></mrow></mfenced><mtext>&#160;molar conductivity&#160;</mtext></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#923;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>limiting</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>molar</mi><mo>conductivity</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>molar</mi><mo>concentration</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>&#160;dissociation constant of&#160;</mtext><mi>HX</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
